## Parked 2026-09-15 07:20

**Goal:** Fix the exit-path ISI that hard-hung the Wii U every time SoH 9.2.3 was exited.

**Stopped at:** DONE and verified on device. User left and took the console off-network,
so no further on-device testing is possible for now.

**State:** SOLVED. Root cause: `gfx_wiiu_shutdown` calls `GX2Shutdown()` during
`gfx_wiiu_teardown`, while `Gui::ShutDownImGui` (Gui.cpp:202) runs
`ImGui_ImplGX2_Shutdown()` only AFTERWARDS — so `ImGui_ImplGX2_DestroyFontsTexture`
reached `GX2RDestroySurfaceEx`, and `DestroyDeviceObjects` reached
`WHBGfxFreeShaderGroup`, on a dead GX2 whose GX2R allocator hooks were already gone.
Both dispatched through NULL. Fixed with `gfx_wiiu_gx2_is_down()` (gfx_wiiu.cpp:83,
flag set at line 514 immediately before `GX2Shutdown()`), checked in both ImGui GX2
teardown paths so they skip ONLY the GPU-side frees. Verified on device 07:12:38 —
both skip lines emitted, `EXIT: exit(0)`, and ZERO `EXC: ISI`. Evidence:
`wiiu/soh923-exit-test-20260915-0505.log` (line ~4922 onward) in the homelab repo.

Also landed this session:
- `-Wl,--wrap=exit` added to `soh/CMakeLists.txt`. It was documented as the hurdle-7
  fix but had NEVER been in the build, so `__wrap_exit` was dead code. Now 9 call
  sites bind to it, 0 to real `exit`.
- `OSGetSymbolName` resolution on the ISI, emitted as a second `EXC-SYM:` line AFTER
  the register line. This is what solved the case in one build.
- devoptab hygiene: `Exit()`/`__wrap_exit()` install a fully-populated `dotab_devnull`
  before `WHBLogUdpDeinit()`; `dotab_stdout` NULL slots filled.
- `__wrap___cxa_throw` bias now derived from `__init` (pinned at 0x02000080 by
  wut-crtfix.ld) instead of a constant that went stale every rebuild.

**Ruled out:**
- **The devoptab hypothesis recorded in commit cab0f12 was WRONG.** Do not retry it.
  `lr=0x011822B0` was constant across builds because it is a fixed offset inside
  `gx2.rpl` — a system RPL. newlib/libwhb are statically linked, so a NULL call from
  stdio teardown would have landed in our `.text` (0x0C000000+) and MOVED between
  builds. Also `devoptab_list` lives in our own `.data` (0x1065a3e4), so no system RPL
  can call through it.
- Restoring the ORIGINAL devoptab pointers is wrong: measured in the linked ELF,
  `devoptab_list[STD_IN/OUT/ERR]` default to `&dotab_stdnull`, whose `open_r`/`close_r`/
  `read_r`/`fstat_r` are ALL NULL — the same defective shape being replaced.
- NULL-callback theory on ProcUI/GX2 is dead: teardown already uses
  `ProcUIClearCallbacks()`, and `GX2SetEventCallback(..., nullptr, nullptr)` is the
  documented clear form.

**Constraints:** Nothing was committed — the user was asked twice about committing and
never answered, so this park commit is the first. Nothing pushed.

